# Themed scrollbars — no default "stock" scrollbar

This app never ships the raw OS/browser scrollbar in product surfaces. Every
scrollable region must use a scrollbar that matches its surface theme. The
styling already exists in [`src/index.css`](src/index.css) — reuse it, do not
reintroduce the default look.

## Per-surface scrollbar styling (already defined)

| Surface | Wrapper class | Scrollbar source | Accent |
|---------|---------------|------------------|--------|
| Staff cockpit (`/spec-ops`, KDS, order-manager) | `.cockpit-app` | global rules scoped to `.cockpit-app` (+ `.dark` variant) | amber on slate |
| Customer order (`/order`, `/track`) | add `ming-scroll` to the scroll element | `.ming-scroll` | red/pink on white-alpha |
| Kiosk (`/kiosk`, `/pos`) | inside `.kiosk-shell` | global rules scoped to `.kiosk-shell` (+ `.kiosk-light`) | kiosk primary |

## Rules

- **Do not** rely on the browser default scrollbar for any scrollable UI
  (anything with `overflow-auto`, `overflow-y-auto`, `overflow-x-auto`, or
  `overflow-scroll`).
- **Cockpit**: scroll areas inside `.cockpit-app` are themed automatically by the
  global `.cockpit-app` scrollbar rules — no per-element class needed. Keep new
  cockpit scroll containers inside `.cockpit-app` so they inherit it.
- **/order surfaces**: add the `ming-scroll` class to the scrolling element.
- **Kiosk/POS**: keep scroll areas inside `.kiosk-shell`; it is themed globally.
- Use `no-scrollbar` **only** for intentionally chrome-less strips (e.g. horizontal
  chip rails), never as a way to hide an otherwise-needed scrollbar on long content.
- When adding a brand-new surface with its own theme, define a matching themed
  scrollbar (thin width, transparent track, rounded accent thumb, hover state,
  and a `.dark` variant if the surface supports dark mode) before shipping.

## Aesthetic baseline (match these when adding new scrollbar CSS)

- `scrollbar-width: thin` for Firefox; `::-webkit-scrollbar` width/height `8–10px`.
- **Transparent track** — no solid gutter.
- **Rounded thumb** (`border-radius: 999px`) with a transparent `border` +
  `background-clip: padding-box` so the thumb looks inset/floating.
- Subtle idle thumb (low-alpha slate/white) that brightens to the **surface accent
  color on hover**.

## Quick self-check before finishing UI work

- Did you add or touch an `overflow-*` scroll container? Confirm it lives under a
  themed wrapper (`.cockpit-app` / `.kiosk-shell`) or carries `ming-scroll`.
- New surface/theme? Confirm a themed scrollbar exists for it in `src/index.css`.
